# Halqah — environment.
# Copy to .env for development. Set the same keys in CranL for production.
# .env* is gitignored: these values never enter version control.
#
# One file, not .env.local: the Prisma CLI reads only `.env`, while Next reads
# both. Splitting the two keys across two files means `prisma migrate` and the
# app can disagree about which database they are talking to.

# Development: the portable cluster from `npm run db:dev` — see the README.
#   postgresql://admin:12345@localhost:5433/halqah
# Production: CranL → Applications → your PostgreSQL database → Connection Information
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:5432/DBNAME"

# Signs the session cookie. Generate one with:  openssl rand -base64 48
AUTH_SECRET=""

# حساب المطوّر (lib/dev.ts) — read-only sign-in on both portals: 2999 on the
# teacher's, 1999 on the student's, with this as the password. Digits only, at
# least eight. Leave empty and the account does not exist.
DEV_PIN=""
